maintainer_comments.body:
Less nested `if` like this?

```C
    } else if (config->data.numeric.flags & SIGNED_MEMORY_CONFIG && value < 0) {
        ll2string(buf, sizeof(buf), value);
    } else if (config->data.numeric.flags & MEMORY_CONFIG) {
        ull2string(buf, sizeof(buf), value);
```

(for context, instead of this:

```c
    } else if (config->data.numeric.flags & MEMORY_CONFIG) {
        if (config->data.numeric.flags & SIGNED_MEMORY_CONFIG && value < 0) {
            ll2string(buf, sizeof(buf), value);

Yes, I guess `!(A && !B)` is more intuitive because you think about what is invalid. We can write like that, but for me it was just harder to read the parentheses.

Another possibility is the more verbose style:

```C
if (config->data.numeric.flags & SIGNED_MEMORY_CONFIG) {
    serverAssert(config->data.numeric.flags & MEMORY_CONFIG);
}
```

Anyway, both are equivalent and we should know this math logic. :)
